#X text 5 10 To train the AI model follow this.;
#X text 4 46 1) Download and install Python last version.;
#X obj 6 95 pdcontrol;
#X msg 6 72 browse https://www.python.org/downloads/, f 42;
#X text 4 185 3) Create a new object [declare -lib py4pd]. Check if there was no error on console., f 89;
#X text 4 136 2) After installation. On Pd \, go to <Tools> menu \, them <Find Externals> \, search for py4pd and install it., f 89;
#X text 25 207 3.1) If there was errors \, you must installed the wrong version of Python! If you are sure \, report the errors on github.com/charlesneimog/py4pd/issues., f 85;
#X text 3 253 4) If there was no error on console \, create the object [py.pip] and send the exact message \, [pip install Openscofo]. Wait for some time (check the Pd console)., f 89;
#X text 3 314 5) Now create the object [py.o.train] \, and check its Help Patch., f 89;
#X text 2 369 5) Basically you put audio of the techniques inside a folder (for example \, a bunch of tongue-ram audio inside a tongue-ram folder) and them press a button on the help patch., f 89;
#X obj 6 579 pdcontrol;
#X msg 6 542 browse https://charlesneimog.github.io/OpenScofo/descriptors/ai/;
