#X text 56 196 NOTE events describes tradicional pitches. It must be defined as NOTE <PITCH> <DURATION>., f 94;
#X text 56 229 CHORD events describes chords \, stable multiphonics \, and others events. It must be defined as CHORD (<PITCH1> <PITCH2>) <DURATION>., f 94;
#X text 56 272 TRILL events describes trill and tremolo events. It must be defined as TRILL (<PITCH1> <PITCH2>) <DURATION>., f 94;
#X text 56 316 REST events describes rests. It must be defined as REST <DURATION>., f 94;
#X text 2 196 NOTE;
#X text 3 316 REST;
#X text 2 272 TRILL;
#X text 2 230 CHORD;
#X text 56 398 PTECH events describes events from extended/percussive techniques that has defined pitches (Pitched Techniques). It is defined as PTECH <LABEL> <PITCH> <DURATION>. Where:, f 94;
#X text 99 436 <LABEL>: Name of the technique (e.g. \, pizz \, tongue-ram).;
#X text 100 454 <PITCH>: The pitch of the note (e.g. \, C4 \, D#5). Required for pitched techniques.;
#X text 99 483 <DURATION>: Duration in beats (integer or float).;
#X text 56 531 UTECH events describes events from extended/percussive techniques **that has NO defined pitches**. It is defined as UTECH <LABEL> <DURATION>. Where:, f 94;
#X text 86 576 <LABEL>: Name of the technique (e.g. \, pizz \, tongue-ram).;
#X text 86 595 <DURATION>: Duration in beats (integer or float).;
#X text 2 398 PTECH;
#X text 2 531 UTECH;
